          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "A 3.3 V LDO (MCUs + sensors) ... produces 3V3 for \"MCUs and Sensors\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "As netlisted, neither MCU has its VDD pins powered, and the MCU +3V3 net is not connected to the LDO output. The flight-control and navigation processors will not operate.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["HSE1", "HSE2", "FCC1", "NAVC1"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.5", "FCC1.37", "FCC1.12", "FCC1.13", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC", "Net-(FCC1-PH0)", "VREF+_FCC", "Net-(NAVC1-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH1)"],
      "observed": "The FCC crystal nets connect to FCC1.5 (PE6) and FCC1.37 (PE7), not its PH0/PH1 oscillator pins. The NAVC crystal nets have no MCU pins on them; NAVC1.5 (PH0) and NAVC1.6 (PH1) instead connect only to capacitors to ground.",
      "expected": "Each 25 MHz HSE crystal should connect to the MCU's HSE oscillator pins. The specification identifies an HSE crystal for both MCUs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(NAVC1-PH0)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PH0\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither processor is connected to its intended external crystal oscillator. The FCC crystal is routed to GPIO pins, while the NAVC crystal is disconnected from the MCU, so the intended HSE clock cannot function.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["FCC1", "UART3_FCC1"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.48", "FCC1.73", "UART3_FCC1.3", "UART3_FCC1.4"],
      "nets": ["UART3_TX_FCC", "UART3_RX_FCC"],
      "observed": "The nets named UART3_TX_FCC and UART3_RX_FCC connect the UART3 header to FCC1 pins 48 and 73, both identified as VCAP pins.",
      "expected": "UART connector signals should connect to MCU UART GPIO pins. VCAP pins should not be used as UART signals or routed to an external connector.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"UART3_RX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC1\") (pin \"4\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"UART3_TX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC1\") (pin \"3\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The UART3 connector is not connected to UART-capable signals. External connection or signaling on it may also disturb the MCU's internal core-regulator VCAP nodes.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are clearly supported by the netlist: both MCUs' VDD pins are unconnected and their apparent 3.3 V rail is isolated from the LDO output. The HSE crystal wiring and FCC UART3 connections also route to incorrect or unconnected MCU pins."
}

